# SD
1. Logistics Department Head is a physical and systemic object.
2. Secretary is a physical and systemic object.
3. Warehouseman Group is a physical and systemic object.
4. Amount of Goods is an informatical and systemic object.
5. Amount of Goods can be large or small.
6. Goods is a physical and systemic object.
7. Goods can be packaged, prepared or unpackaged.
8. State unpackaged is initial.
9. Logistic Company Group is a physical and environmental object.
10. Package Label is a physical and systemic object.
11. Parcel Insurance is an informatical and systemic object.
12. Goods Shipping is a physical and systemic process.
13. Logistics Department Head, Secretary, and Warehouseman Group handle Goods Shipping.
14. Goods Shipping requires Amount of Goods.
15. Goods Shipping affects Goods and Logistic Company Group.
16. Goods Shipping yields Package Label and Parcel Insurance.
# SD1
1. Goods Shipping from SD zooms in SD1 into Shipping Clarifying, Offer Inviting, Logistic Company Selecting, parallel Goods Packaging, Package Label Writing, and Parcel Insurance Taking, and Pick-up Preparing, which occur in that time sequence, as well as Offer Set and Shipment.
2. Secretary is a physical and systemic object.
3. Amount of Goods is an informatical and systemic object.
4. Amount of Goods can be large or small.
5. Logistic Company Group is a physical and environmental object.
6. Warehouseman Group is a physical and systemic object.
7. Goods is a physical and systemic object.
8. Goods can be packaged, prepared or unpackaged.
9. State unpackaged is initial.
10. Package Label is a physical and systemic object.
11. Logistics Department Head is a physical and systemic object.
12. Parcel Insurance is an informatical and systemic object.
13. Offer Set is an informatical and systemic object.
14. Shipment is an informatical and systemic object.
15. Shipment can be normal, special or unclarified.
16. State unclarified is initial.
17. Goods exhibits Amount.
18. Goods Shipping is a physical and systemic process.
19. Shipping Clarifying is an informatical and systemic process.
20. Secretary handles Shipping Clarifying.
21. Shipping Clarifying requires Amount of Goods.
22. Offer Inviting is an informatical and systemic process.
23. Secretary handles Offer Inviting.
24. Offer Inviting occurs if Shipment is at state special, otherwise Offer Inviting is skipped.
25. Offer Inviting yields Offer Set.
26. Logistic Company Selecting is an informatical and systemic process.
27. Secretary handles Logistic Company Selecting.
28. Logistic Company Selecting requires Offer Set.
29. Logistic Company Selecting affects Logistic Company Group.
30. Goods Packaging is a physical and systemic process.
31. Goods Packaging changes Goods from unpackaged to packaged.
32. Warehouseman Group handles Goods Packaging.
33. Package Label Writing is a physical and systemic process.
34. Secretary handles Package Label Writing.
35. Package Label Writing occurs if Shipment is at state normal, otherwise Package Label Writing is skipped.
36. Package Label Writing yields Package Label.
37. Parcel Insurance Taking is an informatical and systemic process.
38. Logistics Department Head handles Parcel Insurance Taking.
39. Parcel Insurance Taking occurs if Shipment is at state normal, otherwise Parcel Insurance Taking is skipped.
40. Parcel Insurance Taking yields Parcel Insurance.
41. Pick-up Preparing is a physical and systemic process.
42. Pick-up Preparing changes Goods from packaged to prepared.
43. Shipping Clarifying changes Shipment from unclarified to exactly one of normal or special.
